From: Steam-Link-PS5
Subject: session: expose the id of the video frame being submitted

The submit callback carries no frame id, so an application cannot call
IHS_SessionReportVideoFrameStage/Complete for it, and the host never gets the
1 Hz frame stats that drive its adaptive bitrate. Record the id right before
the callback and add IHS_SessionLastSubmittedVideoFrameId().

diff -ru a/include/ihslib/session.h b/include/ihslib/session.h
--- a/include/ihslib/session.h	2026-10-08 19:39:55.770948415 -0700
+++ b/include/ihslib/session.h	2026-10-08 19:39:55.805278036 -0700
@@ -202,6 +202,12 @@
  */
 void IHS_SessionStatsSetFullReporting(IHS_Session *session, bool enabled);
 
+/**
+ * The id of the video frame currently (or most recently) passed to the submit
+ * callback: what to report stages and completion for. Valid inside submit.
+ */
+uint16_t IHS_SessionLastSubmittedVideoFrameId(const IHS_Session *session);
+
 void IHS_SessionSetLogFunction(IHS_Session *session, IHS_LogFunction *logFunction);
 
 const IHS_SessionInfo *IHS_SessionGetInfo(const IHS_Session *session);
\ No newline at end of file
